WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
A laptop can support portable experimentation and smaller models but has thermal and power

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:05.960
limits.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:09.560
A workstation or gaming PC offers discrete GPU options and expansion.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.775
A mini PC favors compact low-power service for appropriately sized workloads.

00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:16.995
Apple Silicon uses unified memory shared by CPU and GPU,

00:00:16.995 --> 00:00:21.240
which can make larger model loading practical within total capacity and bandwidth.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:26.111
NVIDIA, AMD, and CPU-only systems use different acceleration paths and software support.

00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:29.380
GPU servers can provide memory, concurrency, remote management,

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.560
and sustained cooling for multiple users.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.420
A private cloud instance can shift hardware ownership while retaining organizational

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.270
network and access controls.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.475
Its data path and provider responsibilities still require review.

00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:45.380
Size CPU, GPU, VRAM or unified memory, system RAM, storage, network, power,

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.200
and cooling together.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.680
Model weights, context cache, runtime overhead, users, documents, embeddings,

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.280
and other applications compete for resources.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.760
Storage planning includes models, knowledge sources, indexes, chat data, logs, backups,

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:58.950
and updates.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.995
Networking includes local access, remote administration, integrations, isolation,

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:03.835
and bandwidth.

00:01:03.835 --> 00:01:06.955
An assistant can be local and still depend on remote services.

00:01:06.955 --> 00:01:10.835
Choose for the first workload with headroom, not the largest imaginable future.

00:01:10.835 --> 00:01:14.360
Measure a prototype on representative tasks before purchasing or scaling.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:19.040
The best platform is supportable, secure, recoverable, and fast enough for real users.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.095
Define availability needs.

00:01:20.095 --> 00:01:24.355
A personal assistant may tolerate manual restart, while a team service needs monitoring,

00:01:24.355 --> 00:01:28.210
controlled startup, capacity limits, maintenance windows, recovery documentation,

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:30.240
and a fallback when the model is unavailable.
